hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2212","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""All of my Ummah will enter Paradise except the one who refuses."" The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, who will refuse?"" He said: ""Whoever obeys me will enter Paradise, and whoever disobeys me has refused (and he will not enter Paradise)."""
"2213","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates:` Some angels came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). At that time, the Prophet (peace be upon him) was resting. Some of the angels said, ""He is sleeping,"" while others said, ""His eyes sleep but his heart remains awake."" Then they began to say, ""There is an example for your companion (i.e., the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him); so present that example."" Some angels said, ""He is sleeping,"" while others said, ""His eyes sleep but his heart remains awake."" Then they said, ""His example is like that of a man who built a house and prepared food (to invite people), then sent a caller (to the people). So whoever accepted the call of the caller will enter the house and eat the food, and whoever did not accept the call of the caller will neither enter the house nor eat the food."" Then they said, ""Explain its meaning."" Some said, ""He is sleeping,"" while others said, ""His eyes sleep but his heart remains awake."" Then they explained the example in this way: ""The house is Paradise, and the one calling towards it is Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Whoever obeyed Muhammad (peace be upon him) has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeyed Muhammad (peace be upon him) has in fact disobeyed Allah. And what is Muhammad (peace be upon him)? He is like the one who separates the good from the bad."""
"2214","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""People will continue asking questions until they will say: 'Well! Allah is the One who created everything, so who created Allah?'"""
"2215","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Allah will not take away knowledge after giving it to you, except by taking away the scholars along with the knowledge. Then people will seek religious verdicts from ignorant ones, and they will give verdicts based merely on their own opinions, thus they will go astray themselves and will lead others astray as well."""
"2216","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until my Ummah adopts the ways of the previous nations, hand span by hand span and arm's length by arm's length (i.e., exactly)."" Someone asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Do you mean the Persians and the Christians from the previous nations?"" He (peace be upon him) replied: ""Then who else?"""
"2217","Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty sent Muhammad (peace be upon him) with the truth and revealed His Book to him. Among what was revealed in that Book (i.e., the Noble Qur'an) is also the verse of stoning."""
"2218","Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When a ruler exercises ijtihad (independent judgment) in passing a judgment and he is correct, then he has a double reward, and when he exercises ijtihad in passing a judgment and makes a mistake, then he has a single (onefold) reward."""
"2219","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) swore that Ibn Sayyad is the Dajjal. I (the narrator Muhammad bin Munkadir) said, ""Do you swear an oath?"" He said, ""Yes! I heard Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) swear an oath about this in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not forbid him."""
